 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Checkout Form Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a checkout form?\", \"a\": \"A checkout form is the record of who borrowed which item and when they promised to return it. Schools use one for laptops and property managers for keys. On a website the same name means the page where a buyer enters shipping and card details to finish an order.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I make an equipment checkout form?\", \"a\": \"List the equipment with its asset tags and decide each loan period. Then describe both in a prompt to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a>. It builds the form and a table of what is out today. To add a field later, ask in the same chat.\"}, {\"q\": \"What does a key checkout form include?\", \"a\": \"Start with the key number, the door or unit it opens, and the borrower's name. Add the time it went out, the expected return time, and a signature. A key control log also records the date each key came back and who received it at the desk.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a free checkout form template?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Several form builders publish a free checkout form template, and printable versions circulate as PDF and Word files. Emergent is free to start as well. The free tier covers building and publishing a form with your own items and loan periods already in it.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is a paper checkout form still worth using?\", \"a\": \"A printed sheet works when one desk lends a handful of items and a pen hangs next to it. Paper cannot send a reminder, and nobody in another building can search it. Keep a printout at the desk anyway, as a fallback for days the Wi-Fi drops.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do checkout forms track late returns?\", \"a\": \"Set a due date for each type of item and decide what happens once it passes. Good checkout forms remind the borrower before the date and alert the item's owner after it. You can also hold new loans for anyone who still has something overdue. With a form built in Emergent, each loan lands in a database you own, where the late ones sort by borrower.\"}, {\"q\": \"What fields does a student laptop checkout form need?\", \"a\": \"It needs the asset tag, the student's name and grade, and a parent or guardian's signature on the take-home agreement. Several districts require that signature before a Chromebook leaves school. A condition check at return ties any damage to the right student.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a tool checkout form track?\", \"a\": \"Record the borrower, each tool's tag number, and the job or site it is headed to. Kits need a parts count at both ends, because a missing battery or bit is easy to overlook on a busy return. A condition note at check-in protects the next person who signs the kit out.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the structure of a library checkout form?\", \"a\": \"A library checkout form tracks titles instead of serial numbers, and loans run for weeks, not hours. Borrowers often take several books at once, which means the form should accept a list. To lend gear for a fee and a deposit, see the equipment rental agreement form page.\"}, {\"q\": \"Which fields does a credit card checkout form collect?\", \"a\": \"A shipping address and card details, because it belongs to an online store, where a buyer finishes a purchase. It shares a name with a lending checkout form, not the job. To take money for an order or an invoice, see the <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/payment'>payment form</a> page.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
}